Body:
`sdk.client.session.infinitySet(...)` is called without `await` and without `.catch()`. If the request fails, this can surface as an unhandled promise rejection and the UI will still proceed as if Infinity mode was enabled. Handle the promise (await + show error/keep dialog open, or at least `void ...catch(...)`).
```suggestion
      onConfirm={async () => {
        if (props.sessionID) {
          try {
            await sdk.client.session.infinitySet({ sessionID: props.sessionID })
          } catch {
            return
          }
```
